    <item>
      <title>Stefano presents at openSUSE conference</title>
      <link>https://mate-desktop.org/he/blog/2013-07-21-stefano-presents-at-opensuse-conference/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 21 Jul 2013 14:46:13 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mate-desktop.org/he/blog/2013-07-21-stefano-presents-at-opensuse-conference/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;On July 20th 2013 &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/stefano-k&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Stefano Karapetsas&lt;svg class=&#34;hx:inline hx:rtl:rotate-270 hx:align-baseline&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;
 &lt;path d=&#34;m9.1716 7.7574h7.0711m0 0v7.0711m0-7.0711-8.4853 8.4853&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;/&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; presented his
talk on MATE at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.opensuse.org&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;openSUSE&lt;svg class=&#34;hx:inline hx:rtl:rotate-270 hx:align-baseline&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;
 &lt;path d=&#34;m9.1716 7.7574h7.0711m0 0v7.0711m0-7.0711-8.4853 8.4853&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;/&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Conference!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The talk introduces MATE to those who haven&amp;rsquo;t heard of it, explains the reasons for
creating MATE, explains the difference with GNOME Classic and GNOME Fallback sessions,
and describes the features and changes added after the fork.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;iframe width=&#34;640&#34; height=&#34;480&#34; src=&#34;//www.youtube.com/embed/H-2WSt5cbR4&#34; frameborder=&#34;0&#34; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>MATE University</title>
      <link>https://mate-desktop.org/he/blog/2013-03-12-mate-university/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 12 Mar 2013 18:58:22 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mate-desktop.org/he/blog/2013-03-12-mate-university/</guid>
      <description>
        
        
        &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://mate-desktop.org/images/blog/c-file.png&#34; alt=&#34;c-file&#34;  loading=&#34;lazy&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;re proud to announce our newest package on GitHub:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/mate-desktop/mate-university&#34;target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;MATE University&lt;svg class=&#34;hx:inline hx:rtl:rotate-270 hx:align-baseline&#34; height=&#34;1em&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34; fill=&#34;none&#34; stroke=&#34;currentColor&#34; stroke-width=&#34;2&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 24 24&#34; xmlns=&#34;http://www.w3.org/2000/svg&#34;&gt;
 &lt;path d=&#34;m9.1716 7.7574h7.0711m0 0v7.0711m0-7.0711-8.4853 8.4853&#34; stroke-linecap=&#34;round&#34; stroke-linejoin=&#34;round&#34;/&gt;
&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MATE University is targeted at all levels of developers (including beginners)
to learn how to develop new panel applets, Caja (file manager) extensions,
Pluma (text editor) and Eye of MATE (image viewer) plugins, etc. to expand
the already powerful MATE Desktop experience. There will be simple and well
commented code, makefiles and tips to use as springboard for new MATE applications.&lt;/p&gt;

      </description>
    </item>
    
